Wireshark Configuration
=======================
A simple form to see the data published by NDS-SDN in the network interface is using the Wireshark application. In order for you to use it, it is necessary that you set a configuration to see the specific data packages. The configuration is the following:

 - Set the network interface (i.e. <b><i>"lo"</i></b>).
 - Set the Wireshark Filter Settings: <b><i>ip.dst==224.0.0.0/4 and udp</i></b>
 - View the data packages in the selected network interface.


NDS-SDN Device driver operation. State machine
==============================================

The NDS-SDN device driver has only one state machine, the device's STM. The user has to change the device state to perform the different driver's operations. When the driver is instantiated, it creates all the basic infrastructure, parses the XML file and creates all the NDS PVs. The name and datatype depend on the specific content of the input XML. If these operations are completed, the driver is set to OFF state. In the OFF state, the user can change the state machine to the ON state. In the transition, the NDS PVs are subscribed to the source PVs. If all of them are subscribed correctly, the driver will transit to the ON state. In this state, the user can configure the PV with the period publishing rate. When the device driver is set to RUNNING state, the topic is published through the SDN API with two different modes: periodically (the driver creates a thread to support this) or every time a PV is updated. This mode depends on the information provided in the XML file with the trigger field. In the transition from RUNNING to ON, the publication thread is stopped if the driver is working in the periodic mode. In the transition from ON to OFF, the NDS-PVs are unsubscribed. Finally, in the destruction of the driver, the resources are freed.
*/